o class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2061\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D461 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"342\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c73\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c69\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6E\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c68\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2061\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D461 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sinh</mi><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"NONE\">⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></div></div></div></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center; border:1px solid black;\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td style=\"text-align:center; border:1px solid black; border-top:hidden;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center; border:hidden;\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"849\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c73\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c69\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6E\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c68\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2061\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D461 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sinh</mi><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"NONE\">⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center; border:1px solid black; border-top:hidden;\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyModerate\">M</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Mon, Oct 12th @ 7:57 PM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:23</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>"
    },
    {
      "dom_id": "question-335127",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"100px\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
